
/*
QUERY NAME: Fall 2026 Students with Orientation Pending Roles

PURPOSE:
Identifies Blackboard Learn users enrolled in Fall 2026
courses whose enrollment role description is
"Student Orientation Pending".

The query retrieves student identifiers, usernames,
contact information, enrollment role details, and
course information.

It excludes deleted records, course numbers associated
with current child course records, and courses containing
the literal identifiers _WC_ or _OC_.

This report can be used to identify students who remain
assigned the Student Orientation Pending course role
within the selected Fall 2026 courses.

DATA SOURCES:

1. CDM_LMS.PERSON_COURSE (pc)
   Contains user-to-course enrollment records,
   assigned course roles, and role descriptions.

2. CDM_LMS.PERSON (p)
   Contains user information, including first name,
   last name, email address, and STAGE JSON data.

3. CDM_LMS.COURSE (c)
   Contains Blackboard course information, including
   course numbers, course names, dates, identifiers,
   and parent course relationships.

TABLE RELATIONSHIPS:

1. PERSON_COURSE.PERSON_ID = PERSON.ID

   Connects each enrollment record to its
   associated person record.

2. PERSON_COURSE.COURSE_ID = COURSE.ID

   Connects each enrollment record to its
   associated Blackboard course.

Both relationships use INNER JOIN.

IMPORTANT:
Only enrollment records with matching PERSON
and COURSE records are included.

------------------------------------------------------------
FIELDS RETURNED
------------------------------------------------------------

STUDENT INFORMATION:

1. student_id
   Extracts the student_id value from PERSON.STAGE.

   p.stage:student_id::string

   The ::string conversion extracts the JSON value
   as a text string.

   If student_id does not exist in the STAGE object,
   the returned value is NULL.

2. user_id
   Extracts the Blackboard username from PERSON.STAGE.

   p.stage:user_id::string

   This represents the username stored in the
   Blackboard Data STAGE JSON field.

3. first_name
   Student's first name from PERSON.FIRST_NAME.

4. last_name
   Student's last name from PERSON.LAST_NAME.

5. email
   Email address from PERSON.EMAIL.

ENROLLMENT ROLE INFORMATION:

6. course_role
   Canonical course role assigned to the enrollment.

7. course_role_source_code
   Original source-system course role code.

8. course_role_source_desc
   Source-system description of the course role.

9. course_role_desc
   Additional course role description associated
   with the enrollment record.

   IMPORTANT:
   The query retains all four role fields to help
   identify how the enrollment is represented
   in Blackboard Data.

COURSE INFORMATION:

10. course_number
    Blackboard course number.

11. course_name
    Name of the Blackboard course.

12. course_start_date
    Scheduled start date of the course.

13. course_end_date
    Scheduled end date of the course.

    IMPORTANT:
    Course dates are returned for informational
    purposes only.

    They are not used to filter the results.

------------------------------------------------------------
DISTINCT RECORD HANDLING
------------------------------------------------------------

SELECT DISTINCT

Removes duplicate rows when every selected
output field contains the same value.

IMPORTANT:
DISTINCT does not guarantee one row per student.

A student enrolled in multiple qualifying courses
will appear once for each distinct course record.

Different enrollment role details or course
information can also produce separate rows.

------------------------------------------------------------
STUDENT ORIENTATION PENDING FILTER
------------------------------------------------------------

The query searches two enrollment role descriptions:

1. pc.course_role_desc

2. pc.course_role_source_desc

The filter is:

UPPER(TRIM(pc.course_role_desc))
    = 'STUDENT ORIENTATION PENDING'

OR

UPPER(TRIM(pc.course_role_source_desc))
    = 'STUDENT ORIENTATION PENDING'

TRIM():
Removes leading and trailing spaces from
the role description.

UPPER():
Converts the description to uppercase.

This makes the comparison insensitive to
capitalization differences and surrounding spaces.

Examples that match:

- Student Orientation Pending
- STUDENT ORIENTATION PENDING
- student orientation pending
-  Student Orientation Pending

IMPORTANT:
Only one of the two role descriptions
must match for the enrollment to qualify.

The query does not require:

pc.course_role = 'S'

Therefore, enrollment records are selected
based on their role description rather than
the canonical Student role code.

The query also does not verify whether a
student has completed an orientation process.

It identifies enrollment records with the
specified role description.

------------------------------------------------------------
FALL 2026 COURSE FILTER
------------------------------------------------------------

UPPER(TRIM(c.course_number)) LIKE '%2026_FA'

Restricts results to course numbers ending
with a pattern matching 2026_FA.

UPPER():
Converts the course number to uppercase.

TRIM():
Removes leading and trailing spaces.

LIKE:
Performs a pattern match against the
course number.

The percent sign (%) allows any number
of characters before the specified pattern.

IMPORTANT:
The underscore (_) is a single-character
wildcard in SQL LIKE patterns.

Therefore, the current expression does not
require a literal underscore between
2026 and FA.

The pattern must match at the END of the
trimmed course number.

Examples that match:

- PSY_101_2026_FA
- ENG_201_2026_FA
- BIO_101_2026-FA

Examples that do not match:

- PSY_101_2026_SP
- ENG_201_2025_FA
- BIO_101_2026_FA_ARCHIVE

IMPORTANT:
This filter uses the course number,
not the CDM_LMS.TERM table.

The query assumes that the course naming
convention identifies Fall 2026 courses.

------------------------------------------------------------
CURRENT RECORD FILTERING
------------------------------------------------------------

The query excludes records marked as deleted.

1. pc.row_deleted_time IS NULL

   Includes enrollment records without
   a deletion timestamp.

2. p.row_deleted_time IS NULL

   Includes person records without
   a deletion timestamp.

3. c.row_deleted_time IS NULL

   Includes course records without
   a deletion timestamp.

IMPORTANT:
These filters identify records not marked
as deleted in Blackboard Data.

They do not independently establish that
the enrollment, person, or course is active.

The query does not check:

- pc.available_ind
- pc.enabled_ind
- p.available_ind
- p.enabled_ind
- c.available_ind
- c.enabled_ind

------------------------------------------------------------
PARENT / CHILD COURSE EXCLUSION
------------------------------------------------------------

The query uses a correlated NOT EXISTS subquery:

AND NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1
    FROM CDM_LMS.COURSE child
    WHERE child.instance_id = c.instance_id
      AND UPPER(TRIM(child.course_number))
          = UPPER(TRIM(c.course_number))
      AND child.course_parent_id IS NOT NULL
      AND child.row_deleted_time IS NULL
)

PURPOSE:
Excludes a course record if another current
COURSE record in the same Blackboard instance,
with the same normalized course number,
is identified as a child course.

This helps remove course numbers associated
with child course records.

CONDITION 1:

child.instance_id = c.instance_id

Limits the subquery to course records
belonging to the same Blackboard instance.

CONDITION 2:

UPPER(TRIM(child.course_number))
    = UPPER(TRIM(c.course_number))

Matches course numbers after:
- Removing leading/trailing spaces.
- Converting text to uppercase.

CONDITION 3:

child.course_parent_id IS NOT NULL

Identifies a course record whose
COURSE_PARENT_ID is populated.

This indicates a child-to-parent
course relationship in the COURSE table.

CONDITION 4:

child.row_deleted_time IS NULL

Only considers child course records
that have not been marked as deleted.

NOT EXISTS:

If at least one matching child record
is found, the outer course record
is excluded from the results.

IMPORTANT:
This exclusion operates on the course number
within the same Blackboard instance.

It is not limited to checking whether
the current course record itself has
COURSE_PARENT_ID populated.

If another undeleted record shares the
same course number and is marked as a child,
all qualifying outer records with that
course number in the same instance are excluded.

------------------------------------------------------------
EXCLUDE COURSES CONTAINING _WC_
------------------------------------------------------------

POSITION('_WC_' IN UPPER(TRIM(c.course_number))) = 0

Searches the normalized course number for
the literal text:

_WC_

POSITION():
Returns the starting character position
when the text is found.

Returns 0 when the text is not found.

Therefore:

- Position greater than 0 = Excluded.
- Position equal to 0 = Included.

IMPORTANT:
Unlike LIKE, POSITION treats underscores
as literal characters rather than wildcards.

The query does not define what WC represents.
It excludes the literal naming pattern.

------------------------------------------------------------
EXCLUDE COURSES CONTAINING _OC_
------------------------------------------------------------

POSITION('_OC_' IN UPPER(TRIM(c.course_number))) = 0

Excludes course numbers containing the
literal text:

_OC_

The same POSITION logic applies.

Examples:

PSY_101_WC_2026_FA -> Excluded
ENG_201_OC_2026_FA -> Excluded
BIO_101_2026_FA    -> Not excluded by these filters

IMPORTANT:
Both exclusion conditions must be satisfied.

A course number containing either _WC_
or _OC_ is excluded.

These conditions inspect the course number
only, not the course name or other fields.

------------------------------------------------------------
COMBINED FILTERING LOGIC
------------------------------------------------------------

To appear in the results, a record must:

1. Have an enrollment role description matching
   Student Orientation Pending in at least
   one of the two role description fields.

2. Have a course number matching the
   Fall 2026 ending pattern.

3. Have enrollment, person, and course records
   that are not marked as deleted.

4. Have no matching undeleted child course record
   sharing its course number and Blackboard instance.

5. Have a course number that does not contain
   the literal _WC_ text.

6. Have a course number that does not contain
   the literal _OC_ text.

All applicable conditions must be satisfied
for a record to appear in the results.

------------------------------------------------------------
SORTING
------------------------------------------------------------

Results are ordered by:

1. p.last_name
   Sorts alphabetically by last name.

2. p.first_name
   Sorts alphabetically by first name when
   last names are identical.

3. c.course_number
   Sorts by course number when both student
   name values are identical.

The default sort direction is ascending.

------------------------------------------------------------
IMPORTANT NOTES
------------------------------------------------------------

- The report identifies enrollments assigned
  the Student Orientation Pending role description.

- It does not confirm whether students have
  completed or failed to complete orientation.

- It searches Fall 2026 courses using a
  course-number pattern, not the TERM table.

- Course start and end dates are displayed
  but do not affect inclusion.

- Deleted enrollment, person, and course
  records are excluded.

- Availability and enabled indicators
  are not evaluated.

- SELECT DISTINCT removes duplicate output
  rows but does not guarantee one row per student.

- The NOT EXISTS subquery excludes course numbers
  associated with undeleted child course records
  within the same Blackboard instance.

- Courses containing _WC_ or _OC_ are excluded
  using literal substring searches.

- Student IDs and Blackboard usernames are
  extracted from PERSON.STAGE JSON data.

- The query does not use CURRENT_DATE().

- Results reflect the enrollment role values
  stored in Blackboard Data - Illuminate
  at the time the query is executed.

*/

SELECT DISTINCT
    p.stage:student_id::string AS student_id,
    p.stage:user_id::string    AS user_id,
    p.first_name,
    p.last_name,
    p.email,

    pc.course_role,
    pc.course_role_source_code,
    pc.course_role_source_desc,
    pc.course_role_desc,

    c.course_number,
    c.name                     AS course_name,
    c.start_date               AS course_start_date,
    c.end_date                 AS course_end_date

FROM CDM_LMS.PERSON_COURSE pc

INNER JOIN CDM_LMS.PERSON p
    ON p.id = pc.person_id

INNER JOIN CDM_LMS.COURSE c
    ON c.id = pc.course_id

WHERE
    (
        UPPER(TRIM(pc.course_role_desc)) = 'STUDENT ORIENTATION PENDING'
        OR
        UPPER(TRIM(pc.course_role_source_desc)) = 'STUDENT ORIENTATION PENDING'
    )

    AND UPPER(TRIM(c.course_number)) LIKE '%2026_FA'

    -- Current enrollment/course/person records
    AND pc.row_deleted_time IS NULL
    AND p.row_deleted_time IS NULL
    AND c.row_deleted_time IS NULL

    -- Exclude a course number if ANY current COURSE record
    -- for that course number identifies it as a child
    AND NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM CDM_LMS.COURSE child
        WHERE child.instance_id = c.instance_id
          AND UPPER(TRIM(child.course_number))
              = UPPER(TRIM(c.course_number))
          AND child.course_parent_id IS NOT NULL
          AND child.row_deleted_time IS NULL
    )

    -- Exclude courses containing literal _WC_
    AND POSITION('_WC_' IN UPPER(TRIM(c.course_number))) = 0

    -- Exclude courses containing literal _OC_
    AND POSITION('_OC_' IN UPPER(TRIM(c.course_number))) = 0

ORDER BY
    p.last_name,
    p.first_name,
    c.course_number;
